<!-- cammap - the pages a search engine should know about.

     Written by hand. Seven addresses do not need generating, and a
     generator would be one more tool for a site that has none. Every
     page that is meant to be found is here; the moderation page is
     not, because its <head> says noindex - it is empty for anyone who
     is not a moderator - and a sitemap that lists a page and a <head>
     that refuses it are a contradiction Search Console reports as an
     error. 404.html is not a page, so it is not here either.

     lastmod is the date of the page's last commit, which is what a
     crawler uses to decide whether to fetch the page again. When a
     page changes, update its line here and commit the two together;
     git log gives the date, and NOTES.md ("Sharing the site") has the
     exact command, which cannot be written in an XML comment because
     it contains a double hyphen. A date that is too old costs a slow
     re-crawl; a date that is too new costs nothing, so when in doubt
     use today's.

     The addresses are absolute, as the sitemap format requires, and
     they name the site's home on GitHub Pages. If it moves to a domain
     of its own they all change - see NOTES.md, "Sharing the site", for
     every other file that carries the address. -->
